##
## Upstream tests to disable
##
## When adding a new filter to this list, please include a short description of
## why the filter is required and create an associated tracking issue if needed.
##

# Brave runs EmbeddingGemma through LiteRT, which returns before the upstream
# TFLite model load that records these histograms. See
# chromium_src/services/passage_embeddings/passage_embedder_impl.cc.
-PassageEmbedderImplTest.RecordsGemmaHistograms

# These tests fail because Brave treats a request that is same-site with its
# top frame origin as first-party, even when its SiteForCookies is null. When
# upstream blocks such a request, IsFullCookieAccessAllowed() falls back to
# BraveIsAllowedThirdParty(), which compares the URL with the top frame origin
# only. See
# chromium_src/components/content_settings/core/common/cookie_settings_base.cc.
# This is intended: it keeps first-party frames nested in third-party frames
# working.
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.ChangeSettings/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.CookiesEnabledFor/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.GetAllForUrlPolicy/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.SetCanonicalCookiePolicy/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.SetCookieFromStringCrossOrigin/NETWORK_000100
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.SetCookieFromStringCrossOrigin/SCRIPT_000100
-CookieManagerTest.BlockThirdPartyCookies
-NetworkServiceNetworkDelegateTest.ClearSiteDataPartitionedStateOnlyForCrossSiteSubframe

# These tests fail because Brave gives a cross-site context ephemeral storage
# when the cookie settings would block its cookies.
# IsEphemeralCookieAccessAllowed() and IsEphemeralPrivacyModeEnabled() report
# that access as allowed, where upstream reports it as blocked or as
# kPartitionedStateAllowedOnly. See
# chromium_src/services/network/cookie_settings.cc and
# chromium_src/services/network/restricted_cookie_manager.cc.
# This is intended: ephemeral storage replaces third-party cookie blocking.
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.CookiesEnabledFor_WithStorageAccess/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.GetAllForUrlEqualsMatch_WithStorageAccess/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.PreferBoundCookieContextForCookiesEnabledFor/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.PreferBoundCookieContextForCookieStoreSet/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.PreferBoundCookieContextForScriptGet/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.PreferBoundCookieContextForTopFrameOrigin/*
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.SetCanonicalCookie_WithStorageAccess/*
-NetworkContextTest.PrivacyModeEnabledIfCookiesBlocked
-NetworkContextTest.PrivacyModeEnabledIfThirdPartyCookiesBlocked

# These tests fail because IsEphemeralCookieAccessible() and
# AnnotateAndMoveUserBlockedEphemeralCookies() return true as soon as access is
# allowed, without the upstream calls that add the WARN_THIRD_PARTY_PHASEOUT
# warning to the inclusion status. FilteredCookieAccessEvents also hits the
# same-site case above. See chromium_src/services/network/cookie_settings.cc.
# This is an accepted side effect: only DevTools reads the warning, and
# restoring it would route Brave's allow decision through the stricter
# upstream check.
-All/RestrictedCookieManagerTest.FilteredCookieAccessEvents/*
-NetworkContextTest.CanSetCookieTrueIfCookiesAllowed

# These tests fail because CookieSettingsBase::ShouldUseEphemeralStorage()
# decides on ephemeral storage without the request's cookie setting overrides,
# so a storage access grant does not keep a cross-site request out of
# ephemeral storage, and the request never sees the cookie the test set in the
# persistent cookie jar. Brave disables the Storage Access API, and its
# browser_tests are filtered as well. See
# chromium_src/components/content_settings/core/common/cookie_settings_base.cc.
# This is intended while the Storage Access API is disabled.
-StorageAccessHeaderNetworkContextParameterizedTest.Retry/1
-StorageAccessHeaderNetworkContextParameterizedTest.RetryABAWithResourceRequestOptIn/*
-StorageAccessHeaderNetworkContextParameterizedTest.RetryAfterInactive/1
-StorageAccessHeaderNetworkContextTest.OptedInViaResourceRequest
-StorageAccessHeaderNetworkContextTest.RequestHeader_Active_TopLevelStorageAccess
-StorageAccessHeaderRedirectNetworkContextTest.RetryThenRedirect/*
